# TeleWire application credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `telewire.credentials` (no .example) and fill in the two
# values. That file is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# With it present, everyone who runs your build signs in with **just a phone
# number** — no API ID, no API hash, no setup screen.
#
# What these are: they identify the *application*, not the account. Telegram
# Desktop ships with a pair of its own. TeleWire still signs in as an ordinary
# user account (phone + login code), never a bot, and ordinary accounts can
# download everything they can already see in Telegram. Telegram simply
# requires an app identity before any MTProto connection can be opened, which
# is why it cannot be deferred until after the phone number.
#
# To get a pair (takes about a minute, one time, free):
#   1. Open https://my.telegram.org/apps and sign in with your phone number
#   2. Fill in any app name and short name ("TeleWire" / "telewire" is fine)
#   3. Copy the "App api_id" and "App api_hash" it shows you
#
# Do NOT publish these. An api_id found in a public repository gets
# API_ID_PUBLISHED_FLOOD from Telegram and stops working for everyone using it.

TELEWIRE_API_ID=
TELEWIRE_API_HASH=
